comment_data.body:
To my knowledge, Vim has to modify `libvterm` in C89 to be compiled with Vim compared to Neovim. Meaning, certain Vim patches for C89 compatibility shouldn't be applicable (normally). That C89 requirement should be loosened by now but I don't know when (ex. v9.1.x?).

Since Vim's `src/terminal.c` and related  files for implementing and testing `:terminal` are also marked as N/A, then it's possible that valid patches for `libvterm` are wrongly marked as N/A for Neovim **IFF** there are no applicable files remaining. Some `src/*.c`,  `runtime/doc/*.txt` remain relevant to prevent these patches from being marked as N/A.

@jamessan Do you know a specific patch that shouldn't be N/A from a `version.c` PR since https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/e15f79c659f8895afdb946333757ad5517329805 and https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/36895 ? I see 5 `libvterm` patches but there could be more.
